    <!-- ── Chairs (2 per table), dark-brown primitives so the colour is fully
         controlled. Origin at the seat centre; the backrest is at -Y, so a chair
         faces +Y at yaw=0 (yaw rotates it to face its table). For dining_table_1
         (served by the robot) the chairs sit EAST/NORTH, clear of the west approach.
         chair_1a/chair_4a (south chairs of tables 1 & 4) are shifted ~0.5m east of
         the table's x: the ground-truth nav has no obstacle avoidance and drives a
         STRAIGHT line from each table's serve point back to the counter before
         heading to the next table (see TABLES/serve in waiter.py) — at the tables'
         original x=4.0 that return line passed within 4-17 cm of these two chairs.
         Shifting east opens ~0.67 m clearance so the robot no longer clips them. -->
